# Repo-root .dockerignore -- three Dockerfiles build from this context.
# api/Dockerfile needs the multi-module Maven reactor: root pom.xml plus
# the rules-engine module api depends on. infra/fly/Dockerfile.public-demo
# (Task 9 Step 5) needs ai/ plus infra/opensearch/'s index mapping and
# search pipeline JSON (corpus/index.py and search_pipeline.py both
# resolve those paths relative to the repo root). infra/airflow/Dockerfile
# (previously built from ../data-platform alone; Phase 4 Task 6 switched
# it to this same root context) needs both data-platform/ and ai/, for the
# same reason public-demo needs the latter -- see that Dockerfile's own
# isolated-venv comment. ui has its own, self-contained build context and
# its own .dockerignore. data-platform doesn't need its own entry here
# even though its own separate `pipeline` service builds it standalone
# (`context: ../data-platform`) -- that build already has its own
# data-platform/.dockerignore, unaffected by this file either way.
#
# infra/ is excluded subdirectory-by-subdirectory rather than as a whole
# tree, specifically so infra/opensearch and infra/fly stay included --
# Docker's .dockerignore cannot re-include a path via `!pattern` once a
# parent directory is already excluded, so this has to be the explicit
# list rather than an exclude-all-then-negate. infra/airflow stays
# excluded even now that airflow's own Dockerfile builds from this
# context -- it COPYs nothing from that directory (the DAGs volume-mount
# in at runtime instead, see docker-compose.yml), so there's nothing here
# it would need.
.git
.claude
reporting
docs
infra/.env.example
infra/airflow
infra/azure
infra/docker-compose.yml
infra/observability
infra/ollama-models
infra/postgres
ui
**/target
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
